toryThe moment we connected to Artemis II to see the moon like never before\nContact us\nGive to ANU\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYouTube\nTiktok\nTiktok\nEngagement\nToggle submenu\nEngagement\nParticipate in workshops, seminars, and challenges to see what Science and Medicine at ANU has to offer!\nHosting an intern\nSchools outreach\nCommunity outreach & STEM boxes\nInternational Relations & Partnerships\n2026 STEM Challenges\nScience Lab: Experiments for home & school\nmeriSTEM\nAustralian Bee Observation Network\nImage\nIndustry engagement \u00bb\nContact us\nGive to ANU\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYouTube\nTiktok\nTiktok\nNews & Events\nToggle submenu\nNews & Events\nFind out what\u2019s happening in the ANU College of Science and Medicine.\nNews\nEvents\nVideos\nOpinion\nStudent blog\nWebinars\nSTEMM Guest Lecture Series\nNewsResearchers use light to reprogram a photonic device\nContact us\nGive to ANU\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYouTube\nTiktok\nTiktok\nContacts\nToggle submenu\nContacts\nFind contact details for all general enquiries and outreach programs.\nCurrent student\nBook an appointment\nFuture student\nFuture student enquiries\nContact us\nGive to ANU\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYouTube\nTiktok\nTiktok\nStudy\nScholarships\nThere are many scholarships available to support the cost of your studies at ANU.\nANU Future Research Talent Award: Chandan's story\nThe ANU Future Research Talent award provides funding for Indian students to visit ANU and conduct a collaborative research project.\nChandan Singh's story\nThe bond of Love\nJharna Chamlagai, who left her birth country of Bhutan as a refugee, says the Love Scholarship is \u201cthe only reason I could come to ANU\u201d.\nRead more\nPreviousNext\nWhether you are a current or future ANU student there are many scholarships available to support the cost of your studies. Donors and benefactors, external organisations and the Australian Government fund many of the scholarships we offer.\nIf you are having financial difficulties there are people to talk to. Contact the Fees and Scholarships Office, the ANU Students\u2019 Association (ANUSA) or the Postgraduate and Research Students' Association (PARSA).\nDomestic students\nLearn more about ANU scholarships available to domestic students.\nGo to the page\nInternational students (ANU funded)\nLearn more about ANU and external scholarships available to international students.\nGo to the page\nInternational students (externally funded)\nThere are many scholarships and sponsorships opportunities provided by government and other organisations.\nGo to the page\nOther opportunities\nCommonwealth Supported Places\nThere are a number of Commonwealth Supported Places (CSP) for domestic students in postgraduate coursework programs offered by the ANU College of Science and Medicine.\nGo to the page\nDr A K Koul Travel Grant\nThis travel grant is to provide impactful support for international undergraduate students whose home country is India, with their associated travel expenses to travel back to India. Funding for this prize has been provided by Ms Himangi Ticku in honour of the late Dr Autar Krishen Koul.\nApplications are now open and will close on 3rd of May 2026.\nGo to the page\nFuture Research Talent Travel Awards (India)\nThe Future Research Talent (FRT) awards are jointly offered by ANU College of Science and Medicine, ANU College of Systems and Society and ANU College of Law, Governance and Policy to students from India.\nGo to the page\nFuture Research Talent Awards (Indonesia)\nThe Future Research Talent (FRT) awards are jointly offered by ANU College of Science and Medicine, ANU College of Systems and Society and ANU College of Law, Governance and Policy to staff and students from Indonesia.\nGo to the page\nSustainable agriculture top-up scholarship\nPhD scholarship opportunity on the co-production of knowledge for sustainable agriculture: Box Gum Grassy Woodlands.\nGo to the page\nDean\u2019s Science Education Commendation Award\nThis page only lists Joint College of Science and Medicine's specific scholarships, prizes & grants.\nGo to the page\nDean's International Science Excellence Scholarship\nThe Dean's International Science Excellence Scholarship is a prestigious scholarship awarded to the very best international students from the College's institutional partners.\nGo to the page\nDirector\u2019s Scholarship for Academic Excellence\nThe Director\u2019s Scholarship for Academic Excellence rewards high quality, top- performing students from the ANU \u2013 SDU Joint Science College (JSC) at Shandong University to study at the Australian National University.\nGo to the page\nExternal scholarships & sponsorships\nThere are many opportunities to fund your science studies at ANU. See below for one that suits your needs.\nGo to the page\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nFacebook\nX\nBlueSky\nYouTube\nTikTok\nBack to top\nAcknowledgement of Country\nThe Australian National University acknowledges, celebrates and pays our respects to the Ngunnawal and Ngambri people of the Canberra region and to all First Nations Australians on whose traditional lands we meet and work, and whose cultures are among the oldest continuing cultures in human history.\nContact ANU\nCopyright\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy\nFreedom of Information\nAccessibility\nTEQSA Provider ID: PRV12002 (Australian University)\nCRICOS Provider Code: 00120C\nABN: 52 234 063 906\nMember of\nHome\nAbout\nDean's welcome\nCollege structure & governance\nFinance\nHuman Resources\nInternational Relations and Partnerships\nMarketing and Communications\nResearch Management\nStudent Services\nInternational Relations & Partnerships\nTeaching & Learning Centre\nAward winners\nGrants & fellowships\nI.D.E.A. (Inclusion, Diversity, Equity and Access)\nI.D.E.A events\nI.D.E.A. resources\nStaff guide on moving to Australia\nStudy\nBachelor degrees\nDouble degrees\nVertical Double Degree Pathways\nMaster 